ut you know  you get a low turnout election and do  you think that's an odd that towards the  Tea Party though that typically tends to  be a little bit more active and turnout  to them well they certainly I'm not sure  if we even say the Tea Party or the  religious right or the far right or what  we say these days because it was  certainly a conservative subset of the  Republican Party that turned out in  primary in big numbers but you know  they're all pretty conservative in their  public and primary so which part was  really activated was the Tea Party or  the religious right or the church groups  seems like more of the latter the tea  party though I think is a movement that  has the divide between its libertarian  side and its Christian conservative side  which i think is not a divide that  became manifest with somebody like Ted  Cruz who I think is closer to the  libertarian side of that tendency then  the Christian conservative side but I  guess we'll see the tension become an  aura ballif if this continues Erika  thank you so much for joining us today  of course thank you for reason TV I'm  Alexis Garcia  [Music]
 

